WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.700
Glad you're here. Welcome to Models and Agents, Episode 110 for July 13th, 2026.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.360
Monday in the AI world, which means a weekend's worth of announcements to catch up on.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.620
Let's go. A new 30-billion-parameter, sovereign MOE model delivers frontier class,

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.760
English and German performance while activating just 3-billion parameters per token.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:32.700
Sufi S30billion A3B launches as a hybrid Mamba transformer trained on 27 trillion tokens with heavy

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:39.260
German waiting. It matches or beats larger dense models on code and bilingual benchmarks while

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:46.160
keeping inference cache size nearly constant as context grows. The model was trained end-to-end

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:52.360
on the German industrial AI cloud and ships with weights, intermediate checkpoints, full data

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:58.220
accounting and training code under permissive terms. This latest openweight release continues

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:04.200
the pattern we saw yesterday of families like Lama and Mistral narrowing the performance gap with

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:11.900
closed frontier systems, particularly on non-English workloads. Builders working on bilingual or long

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.200
context European tasks should test it immediately against current Lama and Mistral equivalents.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:24.080
Next to watch is how the released checkpoints affect fine-tuning recipes for domain-specific

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:30.980
German agents. Stanford's trace system turns recurring agent failures into targeted synthetic RL

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:36.720
environments. The approach diagnoses capability gaps from an agent's own trajectories,

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:44.060
synthesizes one verifiable RL environment per gap, trains a Laura adapter, and routes tokens across

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:54.420
experts. It improves Towsquared Bench by 15.3 points and reaches 73.2% Passat1 on SWE Bench verified.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:01.020
Agent builders should capture trajectory logs and feed them into trace style capability targeting,

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:08.380
rather than generic fine-tuning. Prime intellect released Verifiers V1, which splits environments

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:14.520
into task set, harness, and runtime layers with an interception server that records training ready

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:21.980
traces. Any task set runs under any compatible harness and ships with full prime RL training support.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:30.280
The rewrite under the verifiers.v1 namespace makes agentic RL pipelines modular and reproducible.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.980
RL practitioners can now swap evaluation harnesses without retraining policies.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:43.000
Agent KGV combines dynamic routing and iterative query rewriting for document-level

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:49.800
knowledge graph fact verification, then applies turn-level distillation SFT followed by trajectory

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:58.640
level GRPO. On the long-tail T-Rex split, it lifts macro F1 by 9.4 points over single-turn

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:07.200
rag while cutting average search calls from 3.24 to 1.63. The two-stage recipe transfers reasoning

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:14.000
from a large teacher into a smaller deployable model. Knowledge graph maintenance teams should evaluate

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:21.680
the GRPO policy stage for retrieval cost reduction. Halo adds a course refinement stage plus selective

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:27.100
second-stage latent refinement on a scored subset of tokens with monotonic halting.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:35.640
On the MMLU Pro and GPQA diamond benchmarks it posts the best average among paper-facing methods

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:41.620
while using fewer average refine steps than either fixed one or fixed two baselines.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:47.760
The approach shows that better allocation of refinement, not simply more of it, drives the gains.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.400
Teams running long reasoning traces should experiment with token scoring controllers to cut unnecessary

00:03:54.400 --> 00:04:03.860
compute. Freya TTS is a 183.2 million parameter non-auto regressive conditional flow matching diffusion

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:11.020
transformer that maps directly from a 92 symbol Turkish character vocabulary into the frozen audio

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:22.020
VAE2 latent space. It achieves 8.0 percent WER and 3.0 percent CER on the Freya TREVAL benchmark

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:30.860
while running at 0.11 real-time factor on consumer GPUs. The two-stage post-training recipe locks speaker

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:37.580
identity and covers short utterances for production robustness. Turkish voice agent developers now have a

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:46.080
compact tokenizer free option that outperforms larger open systems. STTT lets the model first identify

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:53.260
relevant evidence spans inside a long context then applies language modeling adaptation only to those

00:04:53.260 --> 00:05:01.860
spans. On long bench V2 and long bench pro it delivers up to 15% relative accuracy gains for Quint

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:12.720
3 to 4B thinking 2507 and Lama 3.1 to 8B instruct. Random span test time training hurts performance

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:18.840
while Oracle span test time training helps dramatically confirming the value of self-guided

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:26.280
selection. Long context rag teams should test the span selection step before full context adaptation.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:33.840
Workspace entropy from anthropics Jacobian lens compliments output confidence for factual

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:41.860
retrieval on pop QA and trivia QA but fails to flag internalized misconceptions on truthful QA.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:49.700
Calibration is highly task dependent and a trivia QA threshold collapses on GSME 2000.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:56.760
The study supplies full notebooks and raw metrics for cross-model validation. Retrieval augmented

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:01.960
teams can add it as a low cost routing signal for high confidence factual answers.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:11.120
Wildtrace supplies 481 tasks over 214 naturally occurring long documents where evidence trails follow

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:17.100
the source's own causal and narrative logic rather than planted needles. It defines seven

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:23.540
source internal evidence geometries and applies multi-stage validation for groundedness and contamination

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:30.340
resistance. Long context reasoning benchmarks have historically relied on artificial distributions.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:36.440
Evaluation suites should add wild trace to measure genuine multi-hop integration.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:43.860
DKCD mines domain knowledge to surface latent causal factors then uses that knowledge to guide

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:50.260
reasoning and produce accurate annotations for graph construction. On two high expertise domain

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:56.520
datasets it materially improves both factor identification and final graph quality over plain

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:03.320
LLM baselines. The three-stage pipeline directly attacks the lack of domain grounding that previously

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:09.940
limited unstructured causal discovery. Domain analysts can now bootstrap causal graphs from reports

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:17.460
without exhaustive manual factor listing. Ant group released SINGARD or NSFA as an open source

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:23.900
safety model aimed at agents and multimodal systems. The release targets security paradigms for

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:30.220
autonomous operation rather than generic content filtering. Agent deployments that interact with

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:35.900
external tools or multimodal inputs now have a concrete starting point for safety layers.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:41.560
Teams should review the model weights and integration patterns for their own guard rail stacks.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:48.160
Okay, let's pop the hood on selective token refinement. Everyone talks about adding more thinking

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:55.280
steps as if extra refinement is always free. In practice refinement is a staged allocation problem

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:01.600
where each additional pass costs full sequence compute. Halo-style systems first run a cheap

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:08.760
core stage across every token then score tokens and apply a second heavier refinement only to a halted

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:15.220
subset. The scoring function learns to predict which tokens still carry high residual error after

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:22.380
the first pass. Monotonic halting prevents later tokens from triggering unnecessary work. This yields

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:28.680
nearly the same token level accuracy as always running two full passes while cutting average applied

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:36.140
steps below even a single fixed pass. The quality gain vanishes once models exceed roughly 70 billion

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:43.000
parameters because the base representations are already low error. So when your traces are long and

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:49.960
most tokens are already stable after one pass selective refinement wins. When every token still needs

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:58.800
work fixed multi pass or full test time training remains simpler. Test Sufi S 30 billion A3B on bilingual

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:04.840
German English code tasks to see whether the three billion active parameter footprint changes your

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:12.180
latency budget versus dense 14 billion alternatives. Run Stanford trace on your agent's recent failure

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:19.680
trajectories to generate targeted Laura adapters instead of generic continued pre-training. Swap in prime

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:26.560
intellect verifiers V1 tasksets for your current agent evil harness to measure how modular run times

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:34.600
affect trace collection cost. Add wild trace tasks to your long context evil suite so you stop optimizing

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:41.780
for planted needles and start measuring real evidence integration. Prototype DKCD's knowledge guided

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:47.880
reasoning stage on your domain reports to surface latent causal factors before building production graphs.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:55.040
Expect more open-weight hybrid Mamba transformer releases as teams replicate Sufi's constant cash

00:09:55.040 --> 00:10:01.380
scaling. Watch for production deployments of trace style capability targeted training once the

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:08.680
synthetic environment generation code is shared. And groups Singard NSFA safety models will likely

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:15.720
see rapid community fine tunes for specific agent tool use policies. Tomorrow keep an eye on how the

